        <h2 id="decide">How to decide what your business needs</h2>
        <div class="chaprule"></div>
        <p>Start with the task, not the tool, and pick the simplest thing that solves it. Write the task down. If it runs the same way every time, automate it. If it needs judgment on changing inputs, and a person can check the result, an agent might be worth a small trial. Then size the gap honestly: an agent only pays off when the time it saves clearly beats its cost and oversight. The fastest way to know where your business actually stands, across data, tools, process, skills, and governance, is to score your readiness before you buy anything.</p>
